WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.030
Well, it is officially that time of the year,

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.690
sleigh bells, candy cane and old St. Nick.

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.030
But one Houston mom is teaching the importance of

4
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:13.020
representation this year and is making sure that

5
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:17.370
all the kids in Texas feel seen this holiday season.

6
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.883
I love this story and this person so much, take a look.

7
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.490 line:15%
Hi, my name is Megan Butler-Coleman,

8
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.300 line:15%
and I live in Houston, Texas.

9
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.330
I am the owner and the founder of a company

10
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.490
by the name of The Black Santa Houston.

11
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.790
And I founded the company about three years ago

12
00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.160
in 2019 for my son, Luke.

13
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.440
It's amazing how children change your lives.

14
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.460
For me, all I wanted to do was

15
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.610
have an opportunity for Luke to take a photo with Santa

16
00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.080
when he was 10 months old.

17
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.750
And little did I realize that

18
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.010
I wasn't actually gonna be able to find

19
00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.820
exactly what I was looking for.

20
00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.430
A person that was a reflection of my family,

21
00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.300
and that had a natural beard.

22
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.610
After a search for more than two years,

23
00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:06.200
when Luke turned almost three years old.

24
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.390
I was able to connect with a very,

25
00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:10.420
very dear friend of mine Oni,

26
00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:14.270
and we were able to start The Black Santa Houston,

27
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:16.920
and now straight from the north pole,

28
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.010
we have created this amazing experience,

29
00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.130
the new tradition in Houston,

30
00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.040
where all families have the opportunity to meet a Santa

31
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.960
that is reflection of their family.

32
00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.510
And that just provides a little additional Christmas cheer

33
00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.108
to a time in which we have a very,

34
00:01:33.108 --> 00:01:36.500
standard image that we usually see of Santa.

35
00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.910
But we are allowing for all families

36
00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.490
to see themselves through Santa,

37
00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.340
through the Black Santa Houston.

38
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.130
Honestly, for me, it's just,

39
00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.750
it has to be over the moon

40
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.630
and we honestly want to celebrate

41
00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.022
Christmas every day. (chuckles)

42
00:01:51.022 --> 00:01:52.060
(audience cheers)

43
00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.810
Megan Butler-Coleman is joining us now via zoom.

44
00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.699
Megan, how are you?

45
00:01:58.699 --> 00:02:00.486
Oh my gosh, hi.

46
00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:04.066
I'm so glad, hi (laughs) oh my goodness.

47
00:02:04.066 --> 00:02:05.510
Megan, you are just my hero.

48
00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:07.480
I mean, what started off as a photo session

49
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.670
for your son has grown into something so meaningful

50
00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:14.680
for so many people in the city of Houston.

51
00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:19.680
Please tell us, what your intention was.

52
00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.730
Thank you so much, Drew.

53
00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:24.220 line:15%
I don't know why it wasn't here in Houston

54
00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.530 line:15%
or just available to all the families,

55
00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.480 line:15%
but I'm just so overjoyed and excited

56
00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.050
that we were able to create an experience

57
00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.110
for families all over Houston,

58
00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.604
even in cities beyond and

59
00:02:36.604 --> 00:02:39.810
beyond photos I just have to tell

60
00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.470
a very special thank you to our photographer,

61
00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.950
because he's able to help capture these moments

62
00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:48.520
and these magical moments with the families

63
00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.610
that are just traditions that are lasting.

64
00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.430
And now we even have Mrs. Claus joining us.

65
00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.650
And so Sandra's on the road.

66
00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.730
He's traveling to cities like Colleen, Texas, to hospitals.

67
00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:04.260
We even have families Drew, flying in from Seattle

68
00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.770
and Oklahoma, Louisiana,

69
00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.370
just to come and have an opportunity

70
00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.810
to just have that magical moment.

71
00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.242
It just overjoys me, It's just so exciting.

72
00:03:14.242 --> 00:03:19.242
I don't know how this is not a standard norm.

73
00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:23.000
I think what you are doing is so revolutory.

74
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.540
I want to see you expand it beyond Texas.

75
00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.360
Thank you for everything you are doing in that state,

76
00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.170
but I'm like, how can we help you build this out?

77
00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:36.130
Because what you have built is so incredible.

78
00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.654
Thank you Drew.

79
00:03:37.654 --> 00:03:39.003
(audience claps)
It's wonderful.

80
00:03:39.003 --> 00:03:40.850
It's just wonderful.

81
00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:42.680
Thank so much for doing this.

82
00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.300
Now, I think it's time actually to meet Santa.

83
00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.998
Can we bring him out?

84
00:03:46.998 --> 00:03:49.622
(upbeat music playing)

85
00:03:49.622 --> 00:03:52.158
(audience cheering)

86
00:03:52.158 --> 00:03:53.575
Ho ho ho ho ho.

87
00:03:58.442 --> 00:04:01.025
Drew, Merry Christmas ho ho ho.

88
00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:09.730
Hello, ho ho ho. (laughs)

89
00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.260
This organization to me is so groundbreaking

90
00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.370
and mind blowing that

91
00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:23.370
I don't know how it's not in every city across the globe.

92
00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.960
And how do we get there?

93
00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.190
Because you see over 500 children in Houston.

94
00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:29.270
Yes, yes.

95
00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.620
And may I ask as

96
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.450
the seed of this most important journey

97
00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:36.300
that you and Megan are doing,

98
00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.646
how do we take this all the way?

99
00:04:38.646 --> 00:04:40.260
Because it's just so important.

100
00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:45.260
Drew, actually it is the joy of the magic of Christmas.

101
00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.220
We want to have our families to have traditions

102
00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.470
that they love.

103
00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.410
And part of that tradition is to have our kids

104
00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.300
to take pictures with Santa.

105
00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.810
So that's some of the things

106
00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.650
that we've talked to Megan about,

107
00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.310
and that's something that we've been doing

108
00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:02.920
for just three years, but it's getting bigger and bigger.

109
00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:05.230
And it's so much more than the picture.

110
00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:08.798
It's a tradition that families really value.

111
00:05:08.798 --> 00:05:11.548
(audience claps)

112
00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.670
This means so much to me.

113
00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:21.330
And you've had such a big impact on the city of Houston.

114
00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:25.620
What have you learned from that model

115
00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.690
that we think we can take elsewhere?

116
00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.402
Drew, I've learned that we have to make sure

117
00:05:31.402 --> 00:05:34.850
that kids at a very young age,

118
00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.740
they begin to see images of themselves,

119
00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.870
regardless of their color, race, or creed.

120
00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.540
That's very important.

121
00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:43.907
So when kids say,

122
00:05:43.907 --> 00:05:45.587
"Mommy, I wanna be a doctor."

123
00:05:45.587 --> 00:05:47.760
"Daddy, I want to be a teacher."

124
00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.180
When they see those images really young,

125
00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:54.150
it's a reflection that they can actually be that one day.

126
00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:57.040
So the sooner they start to see those images,

127
00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.010
the sooner they can know that they can actually do it

128
00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:03.306
and they can become exactly what they want to be.

129
00:06:03.306 --> 00:06:06.056
(audience claps)

130
00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:08.850
If you see it,

131
00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.430
you can be it.
Absolutely.

132
00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:14.480
Now, I hear you do so much charity work

133
00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:19.480
and have a local outreach program coming.

134
00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:22.380
So I would love to let you know

135
00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:25.520
that we want to give you guys $5.000

136
00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.606
to help,
Ho ho ho ho.

137
00:06:27.606 --> 00:06:32.027
By choice, for all the kids.
(audience claps)

138
00:06:32.027 --> 00:06:33.140
We thank you and love you so much Drew

139
00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:34.743
for what you're doing,

140
00:06:34.743 --> 00:06:35.880
for helping us to spread the word

141
00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:39.430
of how important diversity is in a diverse world.

142
00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:40.420
I am in awe

143
00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.387
of what you guys do.
(audience claps)

144
00:06:42.387 --> 00:06:44.430
It is an honor to talk about your program

145
00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:46.560
and let me help expand it.

146
00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.419
Thank you Santa.

147
00:06:48.419 --> 00:06:49.836
Thank you Drew.

148
00:06:50.791 --> 00:06:52.190
And thank you Megan.

149
00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.900
I can't wait to do more.

150
00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.700
Happy holidays, we'll be right back.

151
00:06:56.563 --> 00:06:59.813 line:15%
(upbeat music playing)

